          %p In the introduction of
          %ul
            %li#Mellies06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Andr%C3%A9+Melli%C3%A8s"}> Paul-André Melliès
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Functorial boxes in string diagrams
              %em Computer Science Logic 2006
              in Szeged, Hungary. 2006 (
              %a{:href => "https://dumas.ccsd.cnrs.fr/PPS/hal-00154243"}> hal:00154243
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-00154243/document"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MelliesFunctorialBoxesInStringDiagrams.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p the insight is recalled to have surfaced in the 1970s, with an early appearance in print being the monograph
          %ul
            %li#LambekScott86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Lambek"}> Joachim Lambek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phil+Scott"} Phil Scott
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to Higher Order Categorical Logic
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "linear+type+theory#HistoryCategoricalSemantics"} History of categorical semantics of linear type theory
            for more on this.
          %p A exposition of the relation between the three concepts is in
          %ul
            %li#Harper11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Harper"}> Robert Harper
                ,
                %em The Holy Trinity
                (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://existentialtype.wordpress.com/2011/03/27/the-holy-trinity/"}> web
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20170921012554/http://existentialtype.wordpress.com/2011/03/27/the-holy-trinity/"} wayback machine snapshot
            %li#Eades12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harley+Eades"}> Harley Eades
                , Section 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type Theory and Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://metatheorem.org/includes/pubs/comp.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EadesTypeTheoryAndApplications.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Frumin14
              %p
                Dan Frumin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computational trinitarianism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://prezi.com/fnz-4wzsygiq/computational-trinitarianism/"} prezi slides
          %p
            An exposition with emphasis on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic"} quantum logic
            and the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BaezStay09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"} Mike Stay
              = succeed "," do
                %em Physics, Topology, Logic and Computation: A Rosetta Stone
              = succeed "," do
                %em New Structures for Physics
              %strong 813
              Springer (2011) 95-174 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.0340"}> arXiv:0903.0340
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-12821-9_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-12821-9_2
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#Shulman18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopical trinitarianism: A perspective on homotopy type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/trinity.pdf"} pdf slides
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ShulmanHomotopicalTrinitarianism.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For further references see at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programs+as+proofs"} programs as proofs
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+category+theory+and+type+theory"} relation between category theory and type theory
          %p
            Textbooks on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            and foundations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+language"} programming language
            which connect via the common theme of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            include the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Taylor"}> Paul Taylor
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Practical+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Practical Foundations of Mathematics
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.paultaylor.eu/~pt/prafm/index.html"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Rosebrugh"} Robert Rosebrugh
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets+for+Mathematics"} Sets for Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mta.ca/~rrosebru/setsformath/"} book homepage
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://books.google.de/books?id=h3_7aZz9ZMoC&pg=PP1&dq=sets+for+mathematics"} GoogleBooks
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://patryshev.com/books/Sets%20for%20Mathematics.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Harper"}> Robert Harper
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Practical+Foundations+for+Programming+Languages"} Practical Foundations for Programming Languages
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cambridge.org/us/academic/subjects/computer-science/programming-languages-and-applied-logic/practical-foundations-programming-languages-2nd-edition?format=HB"} ISBN:9781107150300
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+A.+Goguen"}> Joseph A. Goguen
              ,
              = succeed "." do
